Privacy Policy
SnapClip · Effective date: October 13, 2026

In one line: your document content always stays on your device — we never upload it and cannot see it. We only collect anonymous usage data to improve the app, and it never contains your documents.

1. What we collect
Anonymous usage stats — the type and count of feature usage: for example, that a scan was saved, OCR was used, an export or a purchase happened. Never any document content.
Anonymous device identifier — a random identifier generated on first use, used only to link anonymous events from the same device. It cannot be used for cross-app tracking, and it is cleared when you delete the app.
Events also carry the app version and OS version so we can tell versions apart.

2. What we never collect
Your document content, images or scans
Recognized OCR text
File names, file paths or tag names
Any personally identifiable information such as your name, phone or email
3. How we use it
Only to understand which features are used, so we can prioritize development and improve the product.

We never use the data for advertising, and we never sell or share it with third parties.

4. Third parties & tracking
The app contains no third-party analytics or advertising SDKs, performs no cross-app or cross-site tracking, and requests no advertising identifier (IDFA), so it never shows an App Tracking Transparency (ATT) prompt.

5. Storage & transmission
Anonymous usage events are buffered locally on your device and then sent to our own server over HTTPS. Your document content is never part of this.

6. Data deletion
To request deletion of uploaded anonymous usage data, contact us at the email below.

7. Children's privacy
The app is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

8. Changes
If this policy changes, we will update this page and note the new effective date.

